WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.660
Lab 1 runs in the validation-kit
folder of the examples,

3
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.250
in PowerShell 7, and nothing signs in.

4
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.741
Step one imports the module and runs the
check against the fail fixture, a fictional

5
00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:17.675
tenant with both blocks off and soft match
on U P N on, as of October thirtieth.

6
00:00:17.675 --> 00:00:20.350
The status is Fail, with a count of two.

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.297
The details show why:
soft match isn't blocked,

8
00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:27.200
and cloud object takeover
through hard match isn't blocked.

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.837
Those are the two Findings.

10
00:00:28.837 --> 00:00:31.959
The third row is Info:
soft match on U P N is on,

11
00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:34.725
and it can't be turned off once enabled.

12
00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:37.037
It's context, so it isn't counted.

13
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.597
Then the evidence: the source
is Graph, in fixture mode,

14
00:00:40.597 --> 00:00:45.126
and the query names the fixture file
and the URI a live run would call.

15
00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:49.630
A reviewer can tell from the evidence
alone which path a result came from.
